    "title": "One arrested in stabbing on Bluegrass Road - NewsBreak",
    "text": "HUNTSVILLE, Ala. (WHNT) — Huntsville Police have identified a man charged in a stabbing in Huntsville. HPD said Jeffrey Scott Thompson, 45, of Huntsville, was arrested and charged with second-degree assault after the stabbing Wednesday afternoon. HEMSI Spokesperson Don Webster said the incident happened in the 3500 block of Bluegrass Road. HPD said officers responded to the scene at 3:30 p.m. to find a man suffering from a knife wound. Webster said the man was stabbed and transported by HEMSI to Huntsville Hospital Trauma Services. According to HPD Thompson left the scene before officers arrived but was located a short time later near Elm Avenue and Alpine Street. Police said investigators determined that Thompson and the victim were acquainted and had gotten into an argument, which led to Thompson pulling out a knife. HPD said the man’s injuries are considered non-life-threatening. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WHNT.com.",
